    "description": "# napari-movoa\n\nGenerate AI videos with synchronized sound using [Movoa](https://movoa.ai/?utm_source=napari&utm_medium=readme) and inspect the rendered frame sequence directly inside napari as an RGB time-series image layer (`movoa_url` stored in layer metadata).\n\nUseful for synthetic bio-imaging test sequences, teaching animations, storyboard verification, and visualization demos.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npip install napari-movoa\n```\n\nOr install from **Plugins -> Install/Uninstall Plugins** in napari.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Create an API key at [Movoa API Keys](https://movoa.ai/settings/apikeys) and set `MOVOA_API_KEY` (or paste it into the widget's password field).\n2. Open **Plugins -> Movoa AI Video -> Movoa AI video**.\n3. Enter a scene prompt, pick a model (`minimax-h3`, `seedance-2-5`, `veo-3-1-fast`, `seedance-2`, `seedance-2-fast`, `seedance-2-mini`) and aspect ratio (`16:9`, `9:16`, `1:1`), then click **Generate**.\n\n## Related links\n\n- Stylized character workflows: [AI Cartoon Video Generator](https://movoa.ai/ai-cartoon-video-generator?utm_source=napari&utm_medium=readme)\n- Upfront credit tiers: [Movoa Pricing](https://movoa.ai/pricing)\n- SDK and API documentation: [Movoa Docs](https://movoa.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n",
